WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.970
REPLACE is useful for direct literal substitution If
the source system

00:00:05.996 --> 00:00:10.852
consistently uses a known abbreviation and the
business rule says to expand it REPLACE can

00:00:10.865 --> 00:00:18.242
be clear and reproducible But it does not understand
context For

00:00:18.269 --> 00:00:24.413
flexible patterns use regular expressions or a
lookup table rather than stacking many fragile
replacements
